20,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
21,2,,status,Kenji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
22,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
23,2,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
24,2,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
25,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"The bay has a weight limit, and evening hires mean we can't have things that can't be moved or closed.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"People prefer dynamic displays over static cases, and they value having a human presence in the gallery.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Rin,,"The lab is almost empty! Only one person is working there, and the volunteers are mostly town history buffs.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Shipping paperwork has caused delays before, and powered displays have broken down a lot during opening hours.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Transport costs are eating a third of our installation budget, and bespoke mount-making is becoming quite expensive.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Benjamin, does that mean we should avoid loans that need special mounts?","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Rin, if the volunteers know town history, perhaps a local theme would work best.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Rin,,"That's a great idea, Toshio! We need something the current staff can actually handle.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Daisuke, if the bay is weak, we definitely can't have heavy sculptures or big machinery.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,Precisely. We should prioritize exhibitions that arrive with their own supports to save on costs.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,I'm worried about anything too fragile if caterers are walking through the room for evening events.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"If we want repeat visitors, we need a ""working"" element, not just objects behind glass.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Rin,,But we can't do a huge conservation project if the lab is backed up with two hundred pieces!,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Kenji,,And we should be wary of complex electronics if they keep failing and blocking the bays.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we need a balance of low overhead, structural safety, and public engagement.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
